cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived tables, please cite the associated manuscript."
title: "Beer-Flavour-Analysis: above-threshold flavour compounds and trained-panel scores in commercial beers"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, frozen five-fold outer / three-fold inner splits, out-of-fold
  predictions and derived tables for a study of 250 commercial beers
  characterised by 231 chemical properties and 50 trained-panel descriptors.
  The study tests whether exceeding a compound's literature sensory threshold
  is sufficient evidence that routine chemical measurements can monitor the
  corresponding sensory attribute.
keywords:
  - beer flavour
  - sensory analysis
  - sensory thresholds
  - trained panel
  - nested cross-validation
  - multi-target regression
  - chemometrics
  - reproducibility
